<title>INDIA: India to buy 11.1 mln T wheat for sale in 1997/98.</title>
<headline>India to buy 11.1 mln T wheat for sale in 1997/98.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian agencies are expected to buy about 11.1 million tonnes of wheat for sale in the 1997/98 (April-March) season compared with 8.2 million in 1996/97, the government said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The government buys wheat to build up its buffer stocks, which it then uses to control prices by releasing stocks through a state-run distribution system.</p>
<p>The statement said state agencies had procured 8.3 million tonnes of wheat from farmers by June 2.</p>
<p>Total wheat arrivals in the domestic markets were about 9.75 million tonnes up to June 2 compared with 8.88 million tonnes at the same date last year.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +01-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
